terraform init

Initializes working directory (downloads providers & modules).
Example:
terraform init

2️⃣ terraform plan

Shows what changes will be made (no execution).
Example:
terraform plan
terraform plan -out=tfplan

3️⃣ terraform apply

Applies infrastructure changes.
Example:
terraform apply
terraform apply -auto-approve

4️⃣ terraform show

Displays state or plan details.
Example:
terraform show
terraform show tfplan

5️⃣ terraform destroy

Deletes all managed resources.
Example:
terraform destroy

6️⃣ terraform validate

Validates configuration syntax.
Example:
terraform validate

7️⃣ terraform output

Shows output variables.
Example:
terraform output
terraform output instance_ip

8️⃣ terraform state

Manages state file.
Example:
terraform state list
terraform state show aws_instance.myec2
terraform state rm aws_instance.myec2

9️⃣ terraform fmt

Formats Terraform code.
Example:
terraform fmt
terraform fmt -check

🔟 terraform graph

Generates dependency graph.
Example:
terraform graph

1️⃣1️⃣ terraform import

Imports existing resource into state.
Example:
terraform import aws_instance.myec2 i-1234567890

1️⃣2️⃣ terraform refresh

Syncs state with real infrastructure.
Example:
terraform refresh

1️⃣3️⃣ terraform taint

Marks resource for recreation.
Example:
terraform taint aws_instance.myec2

1️⃣4️⃣ terraform untaint

Removes taint from resource.
Example:
terraform untaint aws_instance.myec2
